    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    🔴 MEMBER ORDER IS DELIBERATE: FORMULAS BEFORE THE LOOKUPS THEY SPAN
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    The nine LOI_*__c / PSA_*__c formulas span Primary_LOI__c / Primary_PSA__c, and deleting a
    lookup while a formula still references it is refused. They are listed formulas-first for that
    reason. The Metadata API normally resolves intra-package dependencies; if it does not, split
    this into TWO sequential deploys - the fifteen formulas, then the two lookups.
    ⚠ THE FIVE NDA_*__c FORMULAS SPAN Primary_NDA__c, WHICH IS **NOT** BEING DELETED, so they carry
    no such ordering constraint. They are grouped with the rest only for readability.

    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    THE 17 FIELDS, AND WHAT EACH ONE WAS FOR
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
      Two lookups (2026-08-25) - the things the formulas spanned:
        Primary_LOI__c   -> LOI__c              stamped by the (also deleted) queueable
        Primary_PSA__c   -> Contract_Review__c  same
